From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dodaskot <pessdres@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:16:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 122/131] drm/panel: hx83112f: optionally keep reset deasserted
 in deep standby

The unprepare path puts the panel into deep standby and then asserts
reset. A low RESX releases deep standby while IOVCC stays powered for
the whole system sleep. The vendor JDI driver leaves reset high after
deep standby; prepare() already asserts reset before powering up.

Add a runtime parameter, default off (unchanged behaviour), so both
variants can be compared on the same boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112f.c | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112f.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112f.c
index 1655d6b82..09977fd9a 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112f.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-himax-hx83112f.c
@@ -249,6 +249,11 @@ static int hx83112f_disable(struct drm_panel *panel)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static bool keep_reset_in_standby;
+module_param(keep_reset_in_standby, bool, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(keep_reset_in_standby,
+		 "Leave reset deasserted after deep standby, as the vendor driver does");
+
 static int hx83112f_unprepare(struct drm_panel *panel)
 {
 	struct hx83112f *ctx = to_hx83112f(panel);
@@ -259,7 +264,13 @@ static int hx83112f_unprepare(struct drm_panel *panel)
 	msleep(110);
 	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0xb9, 0x83, 0x11, 0x2f);
 	mipi_dsi_generic_write_seq_multi(&dsi_ctx, 0xb1, 0x01);
-	gpiod_set_value_cansleep(ctx->reset, 1);
+	/*
+	 * A low RESX releases deep standby while IOVCC stays powered. The
+	 * vendor driver leaves reset high here; prepare() asserts it again
+	 * before the rails come back.
+	 */
+	if (!keep_reset_in_standby)
+		gpiod_set_value_cansleep(ctx->reset, 1);
 	hx83112f_power_off(ctx);
 
 	if (dsi_ctx.accum_err)
